findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config implementation uses unwrap_or_default without distinguishing NotFound from
    parse/permission errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented CWE-209-safe Display on CliError. Reviewer verified:\
    \ 'ServerError Display omits response body \u2014 #[error(\"server returned HTTP\
    \ {0}\")] only formats the status code, not the second String field.' Security\
    \ tests confirm at cli_security.rs:12."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: 'TEA wrote header injection tests for tenant_id with CRLF sequences. However,
    the reviewer noted with_tenant() bypass is public (Finding #2), so partially caught.
    TEA tested the validated path but the unvalidated public path remained.'
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that 6 dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. The reviewer noted a toml version mismatch but not the workspace
    inheritance issue.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer Finding #7: 'RawConfig silently ignores unknown fields \u2014\
    \ typos go undetected. Consider #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] to catch operator\
    \ typos early.' Directly flags the config token/unknown field silent ignore issue."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...). The test was written by TEA and passed through dev and review without the
    logical tautology being flagged.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    with let _ = config. TEA wrote 12 config tests but this specific pattern was not
    flagged.
